 of the repo change — `AGENTS.md` gets only the\nhost-agnostic facts (read-only mirror of `origin/main`, refreshed on a lag) so the guidance\nholds for any environment configured this way.","timestamp":1787951230047193415},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Context for this doc change (machine-local, not part of the repo diff): on the operator's\nhost Serena has been re-pointed from the working checkout to a dedicated read-only clone of\n`origin/main`, refreshed hourly by a `StartInterval=3600` LaunchAgent modelled on the\nexisting `com.navapbc.rebar-dev-update`. The updater unlocks the tree, fetches, and relocks\nfrom an EXIT trap, so a failed or interrupted update cannot leave it writable.\n\nVerified before writing this ticket's change: a Serena read against the mirror returns\nsymbols; a Serena `replace_content` write against it fails with `PermissionError` and leaves\nthe mirror `git status` clean; the operator checkout is untouched.\n\nThat host detail is deliberately OUT of the repo change — `AGENTS.md` gets only the\nhost-agnostic facts (read-only mirror of `origin/main`, refreshed on a lag) so the guidance\nholds for any environment configured this way.","timestamp":1787951312614588843},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review PASSED (attestation signed, `verified_at_sha` 9c6dcfda7932...); claimed and\nimplemented. Change pushed for review as Gerrit 2343, commit b76ffae4bd15.\n\nThe one non-blocking advisory (T7/E6) asked whether the section's existing \"This checkout has\nthe Serena MCP server configured\" sentence should be edited rather than left beside the\nappended paragraph. Recorded decision: leave it, additions-only, for two reasons. First, the\nexisting sentence says the MCP server is *configured for* this checkout, which remains true —\nit does not claim Serena *indexes* this checkout, so it is not contradicted by the new\nparagraph, which supplies the missing fact about what Serena reads. Second, the change was\nscoped by the operator to state the mirror and the lag and nothing else; rewording adjacent\nguidance is outside that scope. The advisory was triaged `defer` (priority 0.42 vs a 0.95\nblock line).\n\nGates run in the change's own worktree, all green: `make lint` rc=0, `make typecheck` rc=0\n(683 files), `pytest tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py` 4 passed,\n`check_complexity_baseline.py --check` `new=0 increased=0`. All six acceptance-criteria proofs\nreturned their stated values (section-scoped counts 1/1/1; `AGENTS.md` the only changed file;\n0 deletions; 0 out-of-scope matches).\n\nOperational note for the record: the rebar MCP endpoint was hard-down for roughly ten minutes\nmid-task (`/mcp` returning no response while Gerrit on the same host stayed HTTP 200). The\nlocal CLI could not substitute for the claim — the plan-review attestation is environment-bound\nand the CLI rejected it as `foreign_key` — so the claim waited for the endpoint to recover\nrather than being forced. No force override was used anywhere in this ticket.","timestamp":1787952336195365505},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed: Gerrit 2343 merged at 21:45:28Z with `LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1`, 0 unresolved\ncomments. Gerrit rebased on submit, so the merged commit on `origin/main` is\n`ae203145fa39a153c21b6cba8b25cb5679849ec9` (not the pushed `b76ffae4bd15`); the landed diff is\n+4/-0 to `AGENTS.md` and nothing else.\n\nClose is taking an extra step worth recording, because it is a real seam rather than a mistake.\nClosing through the MCP server is refused with \"no commit references it\": `attach_commits` for\n`ae203145fa39...` SUCCEEDS there (`attached: 1`, so the object is in the server's DB), but the\nclose precheck scans commits *reachable from HEAD* and the server-side root has not advanced to\nthe merge yet. Waiting ten minutes did not change it, and the recorded COMMITS event does not\nsubstitute for reachability in that scan.\n\nThe worktree HEAD *is* `ae203145fa39...`, so the precheck passes locally; the local close then\nstops on the plan-review close gate because the certified attestation is bound to the MCP\nserver's environment and reads as `foreign_key`/`unsigned` here. Resolution being used: earn a\nplan-review attestation in the local environment by running the same gate (`rebar review-plan`,\nno `--force`), then close locally with `--ref ae203145fa39a153c21b6cba8b25cb5679849ec9`. That is\nthe same gate, run where the evidence is visible — not a bypass. No force override has been used\nat any point on this ticket.","timestamp":1787954456348022802}],"commits":[{"sha":"ae203145fa39a153c21b6cba8b25cb5679849ec9"}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787950779680149902,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"5f871544-fad6-4447-a2c0-21439a9d660f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d334-f860-038b-49a4"}],"description":"## Context\n\n`AGENTS.md` §\"Navigating the codebase (when editing rebar itself)\" describes the Serena\nMCP server as operating over \"this checkout\". That is no longer accurate on the operator's\nhost: Serena has been re-pointed at a dedicated, filesystem-read-only clone that tracks\n`origin/main` and is refreshed by a `StartInterval=3600` LaunchAgent (the same shape as the\nexisting `com.navapbc.rebar-dev-update` agent).\n\nTwo consequences follow that an agent reading `AGENTS.md` cannot infer, and that silently\nproduce wrong conclusions:\n\n1. Serena's view is a snapshot of `origin/main`, refreshed on a poll interval, so it can\n   trail current `main` by up to that interval.\n2. It therefore never contains uncommitted work sitting in the worktree the agent is\n   actually editing.\n\nAn agent that assumes Serena indexes its own worktree will read a stale or absent symbol\nand conclude the code does not exist.\n\n## Approach\n\nAppend ONE short paragraph to the existing §\"Navigating the codebase\" section of\n`AGENTS.md`, immediately after the closing \"Cross-cutting change → do **both**…\" paragraph.\nIt states only (a) Serena reads a read-only mirror of `origin/main` rather than the local\ncheckout, and (b) that mirror auto-updates on a lag, so its answers can trail `main` and\nwill not show uncommitted worktree work.\n\nProse only, in the surrounding voice and bold-emphasis style. No table row is added; the\nexisting table is about Serena-vs-grep failure modes, which this is not.\n\n## Scope\n\nIN scope: the mirror fact and the staleness expectation, in `AGENTS.md` only.\n\nOUT of scope, deliberately, and must NOT appear in the change:\n- any warning about Serena's edit tools or write hazards\n- worktree isolation guidance\n- how the mirror or its LaunchAgent is built, located, or operated (machine-local, and\n  `CLAUDE.local.md` / `docs/*.local.md` are git-ignored — this repo change carries no\n  host-specific paths)\n- edits to `docs/code-navigation.md` or any other file\n\n## Portability\n\nDocumentation-only prose in a checked-in guidance file. It adds no code path, no command,\nno CI trigger, and no dependency on any CI provider, scheduler, or host service. The\nguidance is written host-agnostically (\"a read-only mirror of `origin/main`\", \"a poll\ninterval\") so it is equally true for any environment that points Serena at a mirror, and\nharmless where Serena is absent — that case is already covered by the section's existing\n`claude mcp get serena` pointer. Nothing in it can fail to trigger, because nothing in it\ntriggers.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\nEvery proof below is SECTION-SCOPED via the `awk` range over §\"Navigating the codebase\",\nbecause each of these strings already occurs ELSEWHERE in `AGENTS.md` — measured on the\npre-edit file: `read-only mirror` once (line 373, GitHub as a read-only mirror of Gerrit),\n`uncommitted` once (line 447, operator WIP), and `trail` as a substring of `trailer` six\ntimes. A file-wide `grep -c … == 1` would therefore be unsatisfiable or false. Inside the\nsection all three counts are `0` before the edit, so `== 1` after it is a sound proof that\nthis paragraph, and only this paragraph, introduced them.\n\n- [x] The Serena section of `AGENTS.md` states that Serena reads a read-only mirror of\n      `origin/main` rather than the local checkout.\n      Proof: `awk '/^## Navigating the codebase/,/^## Git workflow/' AGENTS.md | grep -c 'read-only mirror'`\n      prints `1` (it prints `0` on the pre-edit file).\n- [x] The same paragraph states that Serena's answers can trail current `main`.\n      Proof: `awk '/^## Navigating the codebase/,/^## Git workflow/' AGENTS.md | grep -cw 'trail'`\n      prints `1` (it prints `0` on the pre-edit file). `-w` is required: `trail` is a\n      substring of the many pre-existing `trailer` mentions.\n- [x] The same paragraph states that the mirror does not include uncommitted worktree work.\n      Proof: `awk '/^## Navigating the codebase/,/^## Git workflow/' AGENTS.md | grep -cw 'uncommitted'`\n      prints `1` (it prints `0` on the pre-edit file).\n- [x] No file other than `AGENTS.md` is modified.\n      Proof: `git diff --name-only origin/main` prints exactly the single line `AGENTS.md`.\n- [x] The change is additions only, so no existing guidance was reworded or removed.\n      Proof: `git diff --numstat origin/main -- AGENTS.md` reports `0` in the deletions\n      column.\n- [x] Out-of-scope topics are absent: the addition names neither Serena's edit tools, nor\n      write/edit hazards, nor worktree isolation, nor any host-specific path or LaunchAgent.\n      Proof: `git diff origin/main -- AGENTS.md | grep -icE 'replace_symbol|insert_after|edit tool|launchagent|/Users/'`\n      prints `0`.\n\n## Testing\n\nThis change is documentation prose, so it carries no unit test; it is proven by the\nacceptance-criteria commands above plus the repository's standing gates, all run from the\nchange's own worktree before push:\n\n- `make lint` — ruff check + format-check (the commit gate), expected to exit 0.\n- `make typecheck` — mypy, expected to exit 0.\n- `pytest tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py` — the module-size contract. This is a\n  CI-only gate that `make lint` does NOT run, so it is run explicitly; expected to pass.\n- `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` — the shrink-only complexity\n  ratchet, expected to report `new=0` and `increased=0`.\n\nA prose-only change cannot regress any of the four, so a failure in any of them is\nevidence the diff touched more than `AGENTS.md` and must be investigated before push, not\nretried.\n\nFinal verification is the Gerrit gate itself: the change is not landed until it carries\n`LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1` (CI green on GitHub Actions) with no unresolved comments.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [x] `AGENTS.md` edited as above; every acceptance criterion verified by running its\n      stated proof command and observing the stated output.\n- [x] All four commands in `## Testing` run and pass.\n- [x] Change pushed to `refs/for/main`, carries `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`, no\n      unresolved comments, and is submitted/merged.\n\n## File impact\n\n- `AGENTS.md` — append one paragraph to the \"Navigating the codebase\" section.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"AGENTS.md","reason":"Append one paragraph to the Navigating the codebase section stating Serena reads a read-only origin/main mirror that refreshes on a lag."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","d334-f860-038b-49a4"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"beaa5ec5-2cd7-4df5-ba69-29c5855b4bac","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[]